---
title: Sheet-Pan Chicken with Jammy Tomatoes and Pancetta
description: Paprika-rubbed chicken thighs roasted on one sheet pan with cherry tomatoes and pancetta until the tomatoes go jammy.
tags: [sheet-pan]
course: main
icons: [drumstick, tomato, bacon]
source:
  name: NYT Cooking
  author: Melissa Clark
  url: https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1021014-sheet-pan-chicken-with-jammy-tomatoes-and-pancetta
servings: 4
time: 45m
---

Heat the oven to 425°F (220°C). Season the @boneless, skinless chicken thighs{1 1/2%lb} all over with @kosher salt{1/2%tsp}(plus more as needed), and place on a rimmed #baking sheet{}.

Smash all the @garlic cloves{9}(whole, unpeeled) with the side of a #knife{} and peel them. Finely grate one garlic clove and put it in a #small bowl{}.

Stir in the @extra-virgin olive oil{2%tbsp}(plus more for drizzling), @fresh lemon juice{1 1/2%tbsp}(plus more for serving), @sweet or smoked paprika{1%tbsp}, @dried oregano{1%tsp}, @?brown sugar{1%tsp} (if using), and @ground cumin{3/4%tsp}. Pour over the chicken, tossing to coat.

Add the @cherry tomatoes{1%pint}(preferably different colors, halved) and the remaining smashed, peeled garlic cloves to the baking sheet, spreading them out around the chicken. Season the tomatoes lightly with salt and drizzle with a little more olive oil. Scatter the @diced pancetta{57%g}(2 oz, or bacon) on top.

Roast until the chicken is golden and cooked through, about ~roast{30-35%minutes}. After 15 minutes, stir the tomatoes and pancetta, but don't disturb the chicken.

Transfer the chicken to plates. Stir the tomatoes and pancetta around in the pan, scraping up all the delicious browned bits from the bottom and sides, and stir in the @fresh dill{1/4%cup}(torn, or parsley or other herbs) and @black pepper{}(freshly ground) to taste. Taste and add salt, if needed, and a squeeze of fresh lemon juice, if you like. Spoon the tomatoes, garlic and pancetta over the chicken to serve.
